{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass on the day that Moses finished.</b> This is written after the blessing of the priests, for so it was: for on the day that Aaron lifted his hands toward the people, the dedication of the altar began. And this verse supports the words of our Rabbis, may their memory be blessed, that Moses would dismantle the Tabernacle during the seven days of inauguration." "<b>And he anointed them,</b> with the anointing oil." "<b>And he sanctified them,</b> by sprinkling." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> \"And it came to pass on the day that Moses finished\" — this is what Scripture says (Proverbs 27:18): \"נוצר תאנה יאכל פריה ושומר אדוניו יכובד.\" The Holy One, blessed be He, does not withhold the reward of any creature; rather, in whatever a person labors and gives his soul over a thing, the Holy One, blessed be He, does not withhold his reward — therefore it says נוצר תאנה וגו׳. Know this for yourself: Solomon built the Temple, and because David gave his soul over it, it is called by his name, as is said (Psalms 30:1): \"מזמור שיר חנוכת הבית לדוד\" — it is not written לשלמה here, but לדוד. And so you find with the Tabernacle: because Moses gave his soul over the Tabernacle, the Holy One, blessed be He, said: I write it only in his name, as is said: ויהי ביום כלות משה — hence you say: נוצר תאנה יאכל פריה. <b>Another matter:</b> ויהי ביום כלות משה — this is what Scripture says (Psalms 51:20–21): \"היטיבה ברצונך את ציון תבנה חומות ירושלים אז תחפוץ זבחי צדק עולה וכליל,\" because in this world they offered sparingly, as is said: ויהי המקריב ביום הראשון את קרבנו נחשון וגו׳ — קרבנו קערת כסף אחת עשרה זהב שעיר עזים אחד ולזבח השלמים בקר שנים — behold the entire offering! What is this like? Like a king who went out on the road, and they would bring before him a meal suited to the road and suited to the inn. The king said to them: Is this how you honor me, and is this what you give me — and I am king and ruler over the world! They said: Our lord, we are on the road and we give according to the road, and according to the inn we have prepared for you; but enter the city, and when you enter your palace you will see how much we honor you. So too when the Tabernacle was erected, all the princes offered a gift: one bowl, one basin, one bull, one goat, one ram. The Holy One, blessed be He, said: Is this my glory? They said before Him: Master of the universe, we are in the desert, and according to the desert we have offered to You; but when You enter Your palace, You will see how many bulls and how many offerings we shall bring before You, as is said (ibid.): היטיבה ברצונך את ציון וגו׳ אז תחפוץ זבחי צדק עולה וכליל — אז יעלו על מזבחך פרים, and not one bull. And so you find with Solomon, when he built the Temple (I Kings 8:63): ויזבח שלמה את זבח השלמים אשר זבח לה׳ בקר עשרים ושנים אלף וצאן מאה ועשרים אלף ויחנכו את בית ה׳ המלך וכל בני ישראל. And likewise in the days of Ezra, what is written (Ezra 6:17): והקריבו לחנוכת בית אלהי דנא תורין מאה דכרין מאתין אמרין ארבע מאה וצפירי עזים לחטאת על כל ישראל תרי עשר — corresponding to the number of the tribes of Israel. <b>Another matter:</b> ויהי ביום כלות משה — Rabbi Yoḥanan said: כלת is in the sense of כלה, for until the Tabernacle was erected the damaging spirits were prevalent in the world. When Moses would go up the mountain he would recite this psalm (Psalms 91:1): יושב בסתר עליון בצל שדי יתלונן — he who dwells in the hidden place of the world, in His shadow shall he lodge. He lodged there one hundred and twenty days, corresponding to the numerical value of צ״ל. He says: אומר לה׳ מחסי ומצודתי אלהי אבטח בו — the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: In Me you trusted; I stand. כי הוא יצילך מפח יקוש — from the snare of David, who was caught to be killed, as is said (I Samuel 23:26): ושאול ואנשיו עוטרים אל דוד ואל אנשיו לתפשם. ותחת כנפיו תחסה צנה וסוחרה אמתו — Rabbi Shimon ben Lakish said: צנה — I make a shield for you and for all who engage (סוחר) in Torah. לא תירא מפחד לילה מחץ יעוף יומם — there is a damaging spirit that flies like a bird. מקטב ישוד צהרים — this is קטב מרירי, regarding which whoever sees it has no life in the world, whether man, beast, or wild animal. How is it formed? Its head resembles a calf, and a single horn emerges from beneath its forehead, and it holds sway from the seventeenth of Tammuz until the ninth of Av. לא תאונה אליך רעה ונגע לא יקרב באהלך — this is the Tent of Meeting: until the Tabernacle was erected the damaging spirits were prevalent, and on the day it was erected, they ceased." "<b>And it appears</b> according to this Midrash, that what it says concerning שחל ופתן, and כפיר ותנין — these are the four classes into which the demons are divided from four persons, as I mentioned in connection with the verse (Genesis 4:22) ואחות תובל קין נעמה. And likewise in later generations in Jerusalem they would recite this song; and so they stated at the beginning of tractate Shevuot: they do not add to the city or to the courtyards except with a king, and a prophet, and a priest, and a Sanhedrin of seventy-one, and Urim and Thummim, and two thank-offerings, and a song; and so Scripture says (Exodus 25:8): ועשו לי מקדש — that is to say, it is like this matter, that all these things existed in the days of Moses, and so you shall do for all generations. And the song is the song against demons — this is what they would recite in Jerusalem to protect from the damaging spirits, just as Moses recited it on the mountain during the work of the Tabernacle. Rabbi Shimon ben Lakish said: Why should I learn this from the book of Psalms? Let me learn it from its own place, as is said: יברכך ה׳ וישמרך — ישמור אותך מכל רע — when? On the day the Tabernacle was erected. Rabbi Yehudah bar Rabbi Simon said: On the day the Tabernacle was erected, Moses entered and heard a voice of splendor, a beautiful voice, a praiseworthy voice. Moses said (Psalms 85): אשמעה מה ידבר האל ה׳ — the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: Moses, peace — I speak peace to them, for I have nothing against My children, as is said (ibid.): כי ידבר שלום אל עמו ואל חסידיו ואל ישובו לכסלה אך קרוב ליראיו ישעו — when? On the day the Tabernacle was erected; for until it was erected there was a contention between the Holy One, blessed be He, and Israel. Resh Lakish said: Why should I learn this from the book of Psalms? Even in its own place it lacks nothing — what is written just before the matter? ישא ה׳ פניו אליך וישם לך שלום." "<b>To establish the Tabernacle.</b> The establishment is ascribed to his name, but of itself it was set up by the hand of Heaven, as it is said (Exodus 40:17–18): ״The Tabernacle was erected.״ And in the Midrash, <b>to establish the Tabernacle</b> — this is what the verse says (Numbers 24:5): ״מה טובו אהליך יעקב משכנותיך ישראל״ — How fair are your tents, O Jacob, your dwellings, O Israel. If 'your tents,' why 'your dwellings'? And if 'your dwellings,' why 'your tents'? Rather, 'your tents' — these are the tents; 'your dwellings' — do not read משכנותיך but rather משכונותיך (your pledges). The Holy One, blessed be He, said to Moses that they should make Him a Tabernacle, so that if they sin, it would be held as a pledge (מתמשכן) against them. Know that this is so, for once they sinned, what is written? (Psalms 78:21) ״לכן שמע אלהים ויתעבר ואש נשקה ביעקב ויטוש משכן שילו״ — Therefore Elohim heard and was wroth, and fire was kindled against Jacob, and He also abhorred the Tabernacle of Shiloh — this is the Tabernacle that was made only so that if they sinned, it would be held as a pledge against them. Another interpretation, <b>to establish the Tabernacle:</b> R. Simon said: At the hour the Holy One, blessed be He, said to Israel to establish the Tabernacle, He hinted to the ministering angels that they too should make a Tabernacle. And at the time it was erected below, it was erected above — and it is the Tabernacle of the Lad (הנער), whose name is Metatron, in which he offers the souls of the righteous to atone for Israel in the days of their exile. Therefore it is written את המשכן — 'the Tabernacle' — for another Tabernacle was erected along with it. And thus it says (Exodus 15:17): ״מכון לשבתך פעלת ה׳״ — The sanctuary, O HaShem, which Your hands established. This far in the Midrash."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:30:37.468589430Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}